Market Challenges
Variable Field Performance
Biopesticide effectiveness can vary according to temperature, humidity, ultraviolet exposure, soil conditions, and pest life-cycle stages. Products containing living microorganisms may require specific storage and application conditions, making field performance and farmer education important considerations.

Limited Awareness and Technical Knowledge
Some growers have limited experience with biological pest-control products and may be unfamiliar with their application requirements. Building confidence requires field demonstrations, agronomic guidance, and clear information about product compatibility and performance expectations.

Market Restraints
Regulatory registration requirements and strain-specific safety and efficacy testing can increase product development costs. Maintaining microbial viability during storage, transportation, and distribution also creates operational challenges. In addition, competition from established synthetic pesticides and price sensitivity among farmers can slow adoption in markets where biological products have higher upfront costs or require more specialized application practices.

